        name: "Hilda Frostmother",
        variantType: "STEVE",
        version: "1.0.0"
    },
    data: {
        ActionData: {
            ActionEventSet: {
                ON_INTERACTION: [
                    {
                        Type: "OPEN_DEFAULT_DIALOG"
                    }
                ]
            }
        },
        ArmorDropChances: [0.08500000089406967f, 0.08500000089406967f, 0.08500000089406967f, 0.08500000089406967f],
        ArmorItems: [
            {},
            {},
            {},
            {}
        ],
        Brain: {
            memories: {}
        },
        CanPickUpLoot: 0b,
        CustomNameVisible: 1b,
        DialogData: {
            Type: "STANDARD",
            DialogDataSet: [
                {
                    Conditions: [
                        {
                            Type: "PLAYER_TAG",
                            Operation: "EQUALS",
                            Name: "nifl_lanterns_done"
                        }
                    ],
                    Priority: 40,
                    Buttons: [
                        {
                            Name: "I will come sit sometime",
                            Actions: [
                                {
                                    Type: "CLOSE_DIALOG"
                                }
                            ],
                            Label: "leave_button"
                        }
                    ],
                    Texts: [
                        {
                            Text: "There now. I did not leave my chair last night and I did not need to. Four small warmths came back across the ice, one after the other, like old friends knocking to be let in. The wedding. The calling on the north ice. A childs first snow. And the far one — the one that was never a townspersons memory at all."
                        },
                        {
                            Text: "I have walked that round more winters than I can stack, and last night I walked it again without taking a step, because Vetra carried the flame and you carried the rest. Sit by my lake whenever the cold lets you, child. Nothing rots in Nifl, and now nothing of yours is sitting out there in the dark either."
                        }
                    ],
                    Name: "Hilda - the lamps came back on",
                    Label: "lamps_relit"
                },
                {
                    Conditions: [
                        {
                            Type: "PLAYER_TAG",
                            Operation: "EQUALS",
                            Name: "badges_gte_7"
                        },
                        {
                            Type: "PLAYER_TAG",
                            Operation: "EQUALS",
                            Name: "no_nifl_lanterns_done"
                        }
                    ],
                    Priority: 30,
                    Buttons: [
                        {
                            Name: "I will find Keeper Vetra",
                            Actions: [
                                {
                                    Type: "CLOSE_DIALOG"
                                }
                            ],
                            Label: "vetra_button"
                        },
                        {
                            Name: "Not yet",
                            Actions: [
                                {
                                    Type: "CLOSE_DIALOG"
                                }
                            ],
                            Label: "leave_button"
                        }
                    ],
                    Texts: [
                        {
                            Text: "Sit by the lake a moment, child. No — I know your face, and I know you do not. That is the cruelty of the cold. It keeps everything, even the things that were taken out of a person on purpose. It has been holding one more memory for you than for anyone else in this town, and it is a heavy one."
                        },
                        {
                            Text: "I hung those lanterns myself, one for every small thing the ice gave back, and I could tell you what each flame keeps with my eyes shut. But a lantern wants a steady hand to relight it, and mine have gone to trembling. Keeper Vetra walks the ring in my stead now — find her down on the shore. The far light has been waiting for the person it belongs to. I begin to think that is you."
                        }
                    ],
                    Name: "Hilda - one more memory than the rest",
                    Label: "late"
                },
                {
                    Priority: 10,
                    Buttons: [
                        {
                            Name: "Thank you, elder",
                            Actions: [
                                {
                                    Type: "CLOSE_DIALOG"
                                }
                            ],
                            Label: "leave_button"
                        }
                    ],
                    Texts: [
                        {
                            Text: "Welcome to the long memory, traveller. In Nifl we say nothing rots — which the young hear as a comfort and the old hear as a warning. Nothing rots. Nothing is buried and stays buried. The lake keeps a ledger the Company cannot audit."
                        },
                        {
                            Text: "See the lanterns ringing the water? I remember every one of them — hung most of them too, back when my hands could hold a flame steady. They cannot any more, so Keeper Vetra walks the round for me, down on the shore. I keep the remembering. She keeps the fire. Between the two of us the lake stays lit."
                        }
                    ],
                    Name: "Hilda Frostmother",
                    Label: "default"
                }
            ]
        },
